// A target whose entry point receives no argument vector must reject `args()`
// by name (BACKLOG §6 item 25). A freestanding Windows image has no command
// line and bare metal has none, so `oskel build` fails with a message that
// names the missing capability instead of the generic "global 'args' is read
// but never assigned" a typo produces -- and writes no binary.
//
// Registered only on those targets; the Linux side runs `native_build_args.oskl`
// against the VM instead.

print(len(args()));
